16. Decision-Making Preferences

When recommending purchases:

* Use Czech/EU availability and prices when relevant.
* Include trade-offs.
* Mention whether a cheaper option is “good enough.”
* Avoid only premium recommendations.
* I often prefer robust, reliable gear over the absolute cheapest.
* For business/chalet use, reliability and ease of maintenance matter more than novelty.

When recommending music gear:

* Do not push too much new gear.
* Help me use what I already have.
* Prioritize workflow clarity.
* Avoid setups that become too complex to actually play.
* Point out if I am solving a practice problem with a gear purchase.

When recommending tech:

* Keep operational reliability first.
* Prefer systems that will still work when guests are present and I am busy.
* Avoid fragile DIY solutions unless the benefit is clear.

When answering cooking questions:

* Give quantities.
* Mention safety.
* Explain how to adjust for children vs hungry adults.
* Consider my equipment: Retigo, shock chiller, GN containers.

